        "item_BywQTq": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<p>In a breakthrough discovery, a renowned Norwegian doctor revived research spanning 50 years by isolating a specialized compound taken from avian egg embryos. The LifePharm LAMININE formula with the proprietary fertilized egg extract has been evaluated by a third party lab showing that it helped repair the telomeres, the protective cap found on chromosomes associated with better cell division, cell longevity and less stress-related damage.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_3Ti4cB": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<p>Studies have shown that sore, inflamed and immobile joints<strong>are associated with shorter telomeres in bone cells. Shorter telomeres are associated with physical aging.</strong>Cartilage is basically a material similar to rubber or soft plastic. Unfortunately, it has no blood vessels or stem cells or the lymphatic system. Once the cartilage is worn away by aging, physical trauma or athletic endeavors it does not have much ability to repair itself. However,<strong>bone cells called chondrocytes near the joint cartilage are activated by FGF2 to help produce collagen, elastin, and matrix proteins that build up cartilage.</strong></p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "spacer_weY4dr": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
