          "settings": {
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<p><strong>Serotonin</strong> is a very important chemical when it comes to our well-being. <strong>Why?</strong></p><p><br/>Because studies have shown <strong>serotonin to help increase cell division and bone metabolism.</strong><br/></p><p><br/>But it doesn’t stop there.<br/></p><p><br/>Serotonin is also vital in helping to <strong>elevate our moods</strong>, and can even help lift us out of depression.<br/></p><p><br/>This is so important because many times we can't do the things we love anymore due to physical limitations… so our serotonin levels take a hit.<br/>And not just once or twice…but over and over again, sometimes for years…<br/><br/>Not only do serotonin levels affect our mood, but they can also affect <strong>digestion, appetite levels, quality of sleep, memory and even social behavior.</strong></p><p><strong>References:<br/></strong><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15131521/?ref=retaildirect&ref=retaildirect\" target=\"_blank\">NCBI - Tryptophan depletion, serotonin, and depression <br/></a><a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5098683/?ref=retaildirect&ref=retaildirect\">NCBI - Anxiety and depression in patients with osteoarthritis<br/></a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29101650/?ref=retaildirect&ref=retaildirect\">NCBI - Regulation of Bone Metabolism by Serotonin</a></p>",
            "link_url": "shopify://products/laminine",
            "link_text": "Try LAMININE Risk Free",
            "link_style": "button"
          }
        }
      },
