    "faq_8ViFB8": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_4KAUfq": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I need to talk to a doctor before taking LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>You may have positive responses to taking LAMININE. Please speak with your doctor if you have concerns or medical conditions. You should not take LAMININE if you are allergic to eggs or fish.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_eMNQWG": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What’s the recommended dosage?",
            "content": "<p>1-4 capsules per day is the recommended dosage. We recommend taking 2 capsules twice a day during the first month of taking LAMININE. After this initial month is over, you can reduce your dosage to 1-4 capsules daily. For convenience, we offer a 120 capsule bottle at purchase so that it may last a month.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_CjKqhe": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are there any side effects associated to taking LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>Natural supplements that don’t contain synthetic substances or pharmaceuticals are usually safe. LAMININE has no known side effects. Some people might experience a stomach disturbance or mild headache, but it is not common and usually goes away within a couple of days. We recommend taking LAMININE with food and a glass of water to avoid stomach disturbance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_LenpmE": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is LAMININE safe for children?",
            "content": "<p>Anyone over the age of 12 can consume LAMININE at the recommended dosage. It's recommended to consult your pediatrician on the safety of LAMININE.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_i4HC6j": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can both men and women take LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>LAMININE will produce health benefits regardless of gender. Both men and women will enjoy its wonderful effects.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_QyxCNp": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can breastfeeding or pregnant women take LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>Talk to your physician if you’re expecting a child or you’re nursing and you want to give LAMININE a try. Though the supplement is safe for everyone, it’s a good idea to have a professional consultation before getting started.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_AH7qjp": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When should I take LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>No contraindications with other dietary supplements or medications are noted.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_n7aQJp": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is LAMININE safe alongside medications or other supplements?",
            "content": "<p>Talk to your physician if you’re expecting a child or you’re nursing and you want to give LAMININE a try. Though the supplement is safe for everyone, it’s a good idea to have a professional consultation before getting started.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_RiqA4Y": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is FGF-2?",
            "content": "<p>FGF-2 is a naturally occurring growth factor found in LAMININE that plays a role in supporting cells of various tissues and some stem cells.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_QDAhK8": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it true that LAMININE can be used to slow down aging?",
            "content": "<p>The FGF-2 and amino acids found in LAMININE work on a cellular level. In addition to stimulating tissue regeneration, LAMININE is also a source of antioxidants that protect the cells against the activity of free radicals, thus slowing down cellular aging. Specific studies have shown that LAMININE supported DNA repair mechanisms indicating healthier cell division and regeneration, which is anti-aging benefit.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_DdWhRA": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How is the egg extract produced?",
            "content": "<p>LifePharm uses a USDA (United States Department of Agriculture) inspected poultry farm in the USA. Chickens are fed high quality whole grains and raised cage-free. Eggs are incubated for a specific time and temperature to extract factors at their peak activity. Eggs are non-GMO and no chemicals or extreme heat is used in processing the LifePharm egg extract to maintain functions of growth factors.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_DQQ8KB": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is there any scientific evidence proving the benefits of LAMININE?",
            "content": "<p>The extract from a fertilized avian egg has been the subject of scientific studies and experiments for numerous decades. It all started in 1929 when a Canadian doctor decided to figure out whether the extract could be used as a natural remedy for debilitating conditions. Extensive research continued in the 1980s and intensified even further after 2000. Numerous basic science research studies and clinical trials have been conducted to determine the biochemically active factors found in the fertilized eggs and how these nutrients can support human health. New clinical studies are being executed all the time, revealing more and more information about the incredible qualities of LAMININE. See research about LAMININE and it's key ingredients.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_MHTBPM": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How much will the delivery cost?",
            "content": "<p>Delivery is free inside of the US.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
